# The CODEOWNERS of the published repository, installed into .github/ by
# publish_to_uxl.sh.
#
# It is kept here, outside .github/, on purpose. GitHub reads CODEOWNERS only
# from the repository root, .github/ and docs/, so a copy under scripts/ is
# inert internally. That matters: 4e5bef87a removed the live internal
# CODEOWNERS because its unanchored patterns auto-requested two reviewers on
# nearly every internal PR, and GitHub offers no way to keep the file and
# suppress that. scripts/ is on publish_excludes.txt, so this template never
# publishes itself either.
#
# Differences from the copy it was taken from: every pattern is anchored with a
# leading / so it stops matching at any depth, and @shaykz is dropped because
# GitHub rejects him as an unknown owner on the public repo for lack of write
# access. Every other owner is kept -- a release PR needs two approvals, so
# shrinking the approver pool is not free.

